#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Add eleven opt-in gcse, sched2, register-allocation, reload, alias, reorg and regmove rules,
first needed by func_0034CEA0.

-frac2-gcse-hash-fp-54: gcse hashes the frame pointer 54 buckets further on.
-frac2-gcse-hash-parm-85: gcse hashes the pseudo register of an incoming argument 85 buckets
further on.
-frac2-gcse-hash-415: the PRE expression hash table has 415 buckets.
-frac2-sched2-pair-units: after reload, once an insn has issued in a cycle, if the best ready
insn uses the same function unit, the slot goes to the best ready insn of equal priority that
uses another unit.
-frac2-sched2-pair-after-higher: -frac2-sched2-pair-units applies only when the insn already
issued in the cycle had a higher priority.
-frac2-equiv-const-keep-length: a pseudo set once to an integer constant (REG_EQUIV) with 7 or
more references keeps its live length instead of having it doubled.
-frac2-reload-const-in-out-reg: an input reload of an integer constant goes into the register
the insn sets, when nothing holds that register before the insn.
-frac2-reload-reuse-until-label: -frac2-reload-reuse-pseudo-reg forgets what each spill
register holds at a code label.
-frac2-output-dep-no-alias-sets: alias sets separate a store from a read, not from another
store (an output dependence stays).
-frac2-unsized-sda-no-cond-slot: a load of an sda-marked variable of unknown size (which the
assembler expands to lui/lw) does not go into a conditional branch's delay slot.
-frac2-regmove-cmove-copy: a conditional move whose destination is neither arm, one arm a
pseudo live past the move and the other zero, gets a copy of that arm into its destination.

Forced on for every USA v1.01 C unit they change 89, 31, 136, 1224, 0, 126, 24, 1, 0, 115 and 9
functions. Three refine another switch: with its base also forced on,
-frac2-sched2-pair-after-higher changes 883 (base -frac2-sched2-pair-units),
-frac2-reload-reuse-until-label 162 (base -frac2-reload-reuse-pseudo-reg) and
-frac2-output-dep-no-alias-sets 808 (base -fstrict-aliasing). Opt-in per-unit models under the
owner's standard of 12 November 2026. Default compilation is unchanged.

Usage: cea0_rules.py <gcc directory>
"""
